# Revised Orientation Day Welcome Email

## Author: Chi Nguyen

### Context:
This document contains the updated version of the orientation day welcome email, revised to correct a typo in the subject line. The email is intended to be sent to all newly enrolled students, welcoming them to the university and providing essential information about the upcoming orientation day. Feedback from a student ambassador and last-minute updates from the dean of engineering have been incorporated to ensure the message is engaging and informative.

---

## Final Email Draft

#### Subject Line:
Welcome to Orientation Day at [University Name] – Get Ready to Begin Your Journey!

#### Body:

Dear [Student Name],

Welcome to [University Name]! We are thrilled to have you join our community and look forward to seeing you at our upcoming Orientation Day. This special event is designed to help you transition into university life, connect with your peers, and explore the resources available to you.

### Key Details:
- **Date:** [Orientation Date]
- **Time:** [Start Time] - [End Time]
- **Location:** [Event Location]

### What to Expect:
- **Welcome Speech:** Hear from our Dean of Engineering, [Dean's Name], as he shares an inspiring message to kick off your academic journey.
- **Campus Tours:** Get familiar with the campus layout with the help of our friendly student ambassadors.
- **Workshops:** Participate in interactive sessions covering academic success, extracurricular opportunities, and student support services.
- **Networking Opportunities:** Meet fellow students, faculty members, and administrative staff.

### Personal Note from the Dean:
"Welcome to [University Name]! As the Dean of Engineering, I am excited to see the incredible ideas, innovation, and passion you will bring to our community. Orientation Day is just the beginning—we are here to support you every step of the way as you embark on this transformative journey."

### Important Reminders:
- **Check-In:** Please arrive 15 minutes early to complete the check-in process.
- **Preparation:** Bring a notebook, a pen, and an open mind.
- **Questions:** Our staff and student ambassadors will be available throughout the day to answer any questions you may have.

We look forward to welcoming you to our campus and helping you begin this exciting new chapter. If you have any questions before Orientation Day, feel free to reach out to our team at [contact email] or [phone number].

See you soon!

Warm regards,

Chi Nguyen  
Communications Team  
[University Name]  
[University Website URL]  

